The self-check runs on every tick, traced or not,
so the one walk the loop check takes on trust is on the tick's path.
It checks the same, so only the loop check's guard on the cut catches it.

Caught-by: loop-bounds

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -546,6 +546,7 @@ static void turn_end(void)
 
 void sched_tick(uint32_t ticks)
 {
+    selfcheck_run();
     tick_advance(ticks);
     turn_end();
 }
